        </div>

       <div class="ch">

    <h1>CMOS Ring Oscillator (3 Stages)</h1>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">A ring oscillator is a chain of an <strong>odd number of inverters</strong> closed into a loop. Each inverter flips the logic level, so after an odd number of stages the signal that comes back to the start is the <strong>opposite</strong> of the one that left. The loop has no stable resting state, so the voltages keep switching: the circuit <strong>oscillates by itself</strong> with no external signal. The frequency is set only by the <strong>propagation delay</strong> of the stages.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Circuit Components</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li><strong>Vdd = 5 V:</strong> supply of the three inverters.</li>
            <li><strong>Mn1, Mn2, Mn3 (NMOS):</strong> pull-down transistors, W/L = 10 µm / 1 µm, Vth = 1 V.</li>
            <li><strong>Mp1, Mp2, Mp3 (PMOS):</strong> pull-up transistors, W/L = 20 µm / 1 µm (twice as wide to balance the weaker holes), Vth = 1 V.</li>
            <li><strong>CL1 = 10 nF, CL2 = 10.5 nF, CL3 = 11 nF:</strong> load capacitors at the three outputs. They slow the ring down to a convenient frequency for the simulation.</li>
            <li><strong>Nodes:</strong> n1 (input of stage 1, output of stage 3), n2 (output of stage 1) and n3 (output of stage 2).</li>
            <li><strong>PMOS wiring:</strong> in the PMOS symbol the drain pin is drawn at the top. The level-1 model is symmetric, so the terminal tied to Vdd simply acts as the source. The pins are therefore wired as (Vdd, gate, output).</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>How One Inverter Works</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">
        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Input high</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>The NMOS turns on (Vgs above Vth) and the PMOS turns off.</li>
                <li>The NMOS discharges the load capacitor, so the output goes <strong>low</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Input low</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>The PMOS turns on and the NMOS turns off.</li>
                <li>The PMOS charges the load capacitor from Vdd, so the output goes <strong>high</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Frequency</h2>
    <div class="ch-formula">
        <span><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1076em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2935em; vertical-align: -0.9721em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mopen nulldelimiter"></span><span class="mfrac"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.3214em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.314em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="" style="top: -3.23em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="frac-line" style="border-bottom-width: 0.04em;"></span></span><span class="" style="top: -3.677em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9721em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose nulldelimiter"></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 2em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 2em;"></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1389em;">T</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
        A signal edge must travel twice around the ring (once to flip every node, once to flip it back), crossing N stages with a delay t<sub>pd</sub> each. Here N = 3 and the measured period is T ≈ 24.9 µs, so t<sub>pd</sub> ≈ 4.2 µs per stage.
    </div>
    <p style="line-height: 1.6;">The delay t<sub>pd</sub> is roughly the time the transistors need to charge or discharge the load: <span><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9012em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">p</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∝</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0715em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0715em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">L</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;">V</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.2222em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">dd</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord">/</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0785em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0785em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. A larger capacitor makes the ring slower; a higher supply makes it faster.</p>

    <h2>Start-Up in the Simulator</h2>
    <p style="line-height: 1.6;">A perfectly symmetric ring has an unstable equilibrium (all nodes at about 2.75 V). A real circuit leaves it because of noise, but an ideal simulator would stay there forever. To start the oscillation, the analysis uses the option <strong>uic</strong> (start from the zero state, without a DC operating point) and the three load capacitors are made slightly different (10, 10.5 and 11 nF). This tiny asymmetry plays the role of noise.</p>

    <h2>Simulation Results (Transient, 0 - 100 µs)</h2>
    <div class="ch-grid">
        <div class="ch-col blue">
            <h3>Waveforms</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Frequency <strong>≈ 40 kHz</strong> (period ≈ 24.9 µs).</li>
                <li>Output swing from about <strong>0.35 V</strong> to <strong>4.95 V</strong>.</li>
                <li>Duty cycle ≈ 53 %.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ch-col red">
            <h3>Phase</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>n1, n2 and n3 are the same square wave shifted by about T/6 ≈ 4 µs from one node to the next.</li>
                <li>Every stage inverts, so n2 falls shortly after n1 rises.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card green-border">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">Three CMOS inverters in a ring form a free-running oscillator whose frequency depends on the gate delay and the load capacitance. Ring oscillators are widely used on integrated circuits as simple clock sources and, because their frequency follows process, voltage and temperature, as sensors that measure the speed of a manufacturing process.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ch-card">
        <h2>Try It Yourself</h2>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            <li>Run the <strong>transient analysis</strong> and compare the curves n1, n2 and n3.</li>
            <li>Double the three load capacitors (20, 21 and 22 nF): the frequency drops to about 20 kHz. Remember to extend the stop time.</li>
            <li>Raise Vdd to 8 V: the frequency rises to about 82 kHz.</li>
            <li>Use five stages instead of three: with the same kind of capacitors the frequency falls to about 23 kHz.</li>
            <li>Make the three capacitors exactly equal: the simulator stays at the symmetric equilibrium and does not oscillate.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

</div>

    </div>
    </div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(560,40)" x="560" y="40" width="440" height="240" class="analysis" name="analysis" description="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;Time Domain&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;dcsweep&quot;:{&quot;param&quot;:&quot;Non&quot;,&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;start&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;time&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;0s&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;100us&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;0.1us&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;ac&quot;:{&quot;start&quot;:&quot;1&quot;,&quot;stop&quot;:&quot;1000&quot;,&quot;step&quot;:&quot;100&quot;,&quot;scale&quot;:&quot;dec&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;de&quot;,&quot;modified&quot;:false},&quot;yAxe&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;n1&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#2196f3&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;n2&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#ea2e2e&quot;},{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;n3&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#11d031&quot;}],&quot;xAxe&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;None&quot;,&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#000000&quot;,&quot;used&quot;:false},&quot;layout&quot;:{&quot;margin&quot;:{&quot;l&quot;:35,&quot;r&quot;:25,&quot;b&quot;:80,&quot;t&quot;:35},&quot;font&quot;:{&quot;color&quot;:&quot;#333333&quot;,&quot;size&quot;:11,&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;},&quot;paper_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#ffffff&quot;,&quot;plot_bgcolor&quot;:&quot;#f8f8f8&quot;,&quot;bordercolor&quot;:&quot;#cccccc&quot;,&quot;yaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;xaxis&quot;:{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;linear&quot;,&quot;gridcolor&quot;:&quot;#e0e0e0&quot;,&quot;showgrid&quot;:true},&quot;showlegend&quot;:true,&quot;grid&quot;:{&quot;rows&quot;:1,&quot;columns&quot;:1,&quot;pattern&quot;:&quot;independent&quot;,&quot;roworder&quot;:&quot;bottom to top&quot;}},&quot;options&quot